 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your farm has a well, but your kitchen sink is bone dry.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you carry buckets from the well, twenty trips a day.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Your back gives up first.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you install a hand pump on the well.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Better, but you still have to pump every time you want a glass of water.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you put a big tank next to the house, and fill it once a day. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But when you open the tap, the water barely dribbles out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Water only pushes as hard as the height above it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you lift the tank onto steel legs, six meters up.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every ten meters of height gives you about one bar of pressure.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now the tap blasts.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But in the first storm, the full tank sways like a tree.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you add cross braces between the legs.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And one day you forget the pump running, and water pours over the top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you add a float switch that shuts the pump off when it's full.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "That's why water towers sit on hills and rooftops all over the world.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a water tower. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
